  (text
    "1. Function: Passive red indicators show VDCIN, BUCK_3V3 before\nJP1, and LDO_3V3 after JP1. This distinguishes converter output\nfrom the jumper-fed LDO rail. A lit LED does not confirm rail\naccuracy, power-good, sequencing, or communication. Each branch\nadds about 1 mA at nominal voltage. No GPIO, USB, 1.8 V rail,\nor signal is loaded."
    (at 694 353 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "4a0daee0-d4fe-4dbb-83db-7164c9996a6e"))
  (text
    "2. Source / changes: These series resistor/LED circuits were\ndesigned by Codex using component datasheets; they are not a\nmanufacturer application circuit. Newly added to carrier V24:\nInherited R600=10k, R601=R602=1.5k (Vishay, 1%);\nD600-D602=Kingbright APT1608LSECK/J3-PRV. Each rail feeds\nresistor pin 1; resistor pin 2 feeds LED anode 2; cathode 1\nreturns to DGND. Existing circuit connections are retained.\n\nKingbright DSAN8387 / 1203014455, Rev V.6A (25 Mar 2021),\npp1-3: ratings, polarity, and recommended solder pattern.\nhttps://www.kingbrightusa.com/images/catalog/SPEC/\nAPT1608LSECK-J3-PRV.pdf\nVishay D/CRCW e3, document 20035, Rev 14-Apr-2026, pp1-3:\nratings, standard 0805 operation, and ordering code.\nhttps://www.vishay.com/docs/20035/dcrcwe3.pdf\n\nNominal currents are calculated, not measured. LED brightness\nat low current, actual rail extremes, assembly polarity, and\npowered rail/ripple/thermal behavior remain unverified.\nRemove JP1 before externally driving LDO_3V3.\nV41: R601/R602 now UNI-ROYAL 0805W8F1501T5E,\n1.5k/1%, 100ppm/K, 125mW standard, 0805. At 3.63V\nand shorted LED, calculated dissipation is 8.87mW.\nRoyalohm Thick Film Chip Resistors, PDF pp1-3\n(printed pp10-12): ratings, dimensions, order code.\nhttps://www.royalohm.com/assets/pdf/products/smd/1.pdf\nGeneral-purpose grade; no AEC-Q200 claim.\nConnections, resistor value and copper remain unchanged."
    (at 694 377 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "87bb0035-6d43-4249-b52b-36d1c3c47e64"))
  (text
    "2. Source / changes: Inherited Gerald LDO pin map; Codex designed this carrier integration, not a manufacturer"
    (at 418.5 81.2 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "9a12ecb8-5043-4669-ab96-967948b7d498"))
  (text
    "application circuit. Oct 2 Gerald native source and the V19 source ZIP differ; confirm the physical LDO revision."
    (at 418.5 84.6 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "e0a40c34-06f0-4ed5-9577-67e43e168c50"))
  (text
    "Opal Kelly XEM8305 Expansion Connectors, MC1/MC2/MC3 tables: https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8305/expansion-connectors/"
    (at 418.5 88.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "9e1384ce-c9f4-4c31-a4f5-439a6082b53d"))
  (text
    "Hirose DF40 Series catalog, Jan 2025, pp5-6,9: https://www.hirose.com/en/product/series/DF40 ."
    (at 418.5 91.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "f7ffad3c-debc-43bb-b9a9-2221a14e1846"))
  (text
    "Samtec ERF6 recommended PCB layout, Rev C (18 Feb 2022), sheet1 Fig1 and Table1:"
    (at 418.5 94.8 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "a02cd8c7-fee4-426e-b551-e367bb91c69c"))
  (text
    "https://suddendocs.samtec.com/prints/erf6-xx-xx.x-x-dv-a-xx-k-xr-footprint.pdf"
    (at 418.5 98.2 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "7dc32144-6b77-4111-832b-8b8f65973cca"))
  (text
    "V26: Codex corrected all six MC1/MC2/MC3 -A locating holes from 1.20 to 0.95 mm; finished NPTH tolerance +/-0.05 mm."
    (at 418.5 101.6 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "5faa56ae-5d12-4a7b-9b17-2e93159d0e37"))
  (text
    "Contact centers, copper pads, circuit pin maps and tracks are retained. Actual assembly fit is not yet verified."
    (at 418.5 105.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left))
    (uuid "686d8fe2-cb22-4fad-98e2-990f9cffccbf"))
